  "forum_transcript": [
    {
      "episode_id": "VR-488475",
      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Juror-2 note on the ledger arithmetic (RW-114, 14 Oct): net dispatches 8+5+6+4 = 23 rolls; receipts 6+5+6 = 17 rolls. ORD-7788 (-7) was cancelled at 10:02 and reversed, so it is not a net movement. Cross-check: opening 52 - 23 + 17 = 46, which matches the recorded closing stock of 46 and the 15 Oct cycle count of 46. On the ledger as submitted, RW-114 dispatches (23) exceed receipts (17). Uncertainties: the ledger is the only evidence in the case; if further receipts or adjustments existed outside this record, the conclusion could change.",
          "content_hash": "0x7ee86cf9d3e00aed5b521090600255f8e8974d84cf31cce6d3efc56fa099c9f4",
          "created_at_ms": 1793320802377,
          "message_id": "2ef4b8dc-8353-4dbb-8e17-555809779145",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Checked the 14 October Riverside DC ledger for RW-114 (stretch hood film, 1.5 m). Receipts: GRN-3301 +6, GRN-3303 +5, GRN-3304 +6 = 17 rolls. Dispatches: ORD-7781 8, ORD-7784 5, ORD-7790 6, ORD-7792 4 = 23 rolls. ORD-7788 (7 rolls) was cancelled at 10:02 with the units returned to the bin and the movement reversed, so it is not a dispatch. Dispatched 23 > received 17 (net -6), and 52 opening - 23 + 17 = 46 matches both the recorded closing stock and the 15 October 06:30 cycle count of 46. The claim is supported by the ledger, so no challenge from me.",
          "content_hash": "0x95cf00a33bbddcd8cc85bcd53a9cda9e64b8bd3e2a1b7fa1bc0f49105f241a34",
          "created_at_ms": 1793320883271,
          "message_id": "f67293df-d6df-49f9-b8fc-2eb982564876",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-3 independent check of the same ledger (RW-114, 14 Oct). Opening 52 rolls. Net dispatches: ORD-7781 -8, ORD-7784 -5, ORD-7790 -6, ORD-7792 -4 = 23 rolls out. ORD-7788 -7 is excluded: the note records it cancelled at 10:02 with the units returned to the bin and the movement reversed, so it is not a net movement. Receipts: GRN-3301 +6, GRN-3303 +5, GRN-3304 +6 = 17 rolls in. 52 - 23 + 17 = 46, which agrees with the 22:00 closing stock and the 15 Oct 06:30 cycle count of 46, so the recorded movements are internally consistent and complete as submitted. GRN-3302 (+40 packs) and ORD-7795 (-12 packs) are RW-209 and do not affect RW-114. Two uncertainties. (1) 'Received' can mean receipts into stock (17) or deliveries accepted from suppliers; dispatches exceed receipts by 6 rolls on the first reading and by 23 on the second. The direction is the same either way but the margin is not. (2) This ledger is the only document in the case; receipts or adjustments outside it would change the result. On the record as submitted I find no arithmetic basis to dispute the claim.",
          "content_hash": "0xb3e2354023d88bbb47ee948cbe391b98b83047f64d8ef8a0fbebb18f0f059722",
          "created_at_ms": 1793320883791,
          "message_id": "0ee3cada-6b1f-4b6f-9d16-29ee06962c35",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-1 independent check of the RW-114 entries in the 14 October Riverside DC ledger. Opening 52 rolls. Net dispatches: ORD-7781 -8, ORD-7784 -5, ORD-7790 -6, ORD-7792 -4 = 23 rolls out. ORD-7788 (-7) is excluded as a net movement because the note records it cancelled at 10:02 with the units returned to the bin and the movement reversed. Receipts: GRN-3301 +6, GRN-3303 +5, GRN-3304 +6 = 17 rolls in. Cross-check: 52 - 23 + 17 = 46, which matches the 22:00 closing stock and the 15 October 06:30 cycle count of 46. GRN-3302 and ORD-7795 are RW-209 and do not affect RW-114. Dispatched (23) exceeds received (17) by 6 rolls, and the direction is unchanged (30 vs 17) even if the cancelled ORD-7788 were counted as a dispatch. Uncertainties: the ledger is the only document in the case, and 'received' could be read as supplier deliveries accepted rather than receipts into stock (the margin differs, the direction does not); receipts or adjustments outside this record would change the conclusion. On the record as submitted I find the claim supported.",
          "content_hash": "0xcf4bc8102148ccec14edfc7fa78b15b9dfbf821500b96a9df97607e77cb8d56f",
          "created_at_ms": 1793320916942,
          "message_id": "2e5bbff8-b363-431c-9916-4b79ac085fe0",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 4
        },
        {
          "content": "Adding the uncertainty on my own check, since it should be on the record: 'received' could be read as receipts into stock (17 rolls) or as supplier deliveries accepted; the margin differs (dispatches exceed receipts by 6, or 23, depending on the reading), but the direction of the claim is unchanged either way. The 14 October ledger is the only document available to me; receipts, returns, or adjustments recorded outside it would change the conclusion. On the record as submitted, the claim stands and I am not challenging.",
          "content_hash": "0x29c0d076ac835e5debf6acc276bcbfad8651c8ea94749ce262513d21f8c826f3",
          "created_at_ms": 1793320970130,
          "message_id": "f726d592-7291-4d01-90ac-b28c42e44a4c",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 5
        }
      ],
      "next_after": 5
    }
  ],
